WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:04.430
Baby Yoda giveth, and Baby Yoda taketh away.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.620
CNBC is reporting that Disney's failure to
have toys based on The Mandalorian's Baby

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:16.039
Yoda available for the 2019 holiday season
has resulted in a loss of up to $2.7 million,

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:19.950
despite the fact that action figures and plushies
are available for pre-order.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.810
"Because of all the secrecy that was surrounding
the series before it came out, Hasbro was

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.990
unable to make Baby Yoda merchandise in time
for the holidays."

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.789
The loss was a calculated one though.

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:35.910
The Disney+ series' creator, Jon Favreau,
has recently revealed that he was moved to

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.570
implore the House of Mouse to keep Baby Yoda
a secret up until his reveal at the end of

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.490
The Mandalorian's first episode.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:47.510
He was inspired by a conversation he had on
the set of Disney's live-action The Lion King

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:52.710
remake with star Donald Glover, who pointed
out that these days, audiences are used to

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:57.210
knowing pretty much everything about every
hot new property before it's even available

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.380
to the public.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.580
Since the element of surprise has become so
scarce, Glover reasoned, it's become a commodity.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.520
As an example, the actor pointed to the recent
works of pop superstar Beyoncé, who has been

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.430
known to drop albums online with absolutely
no prior notice.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:18.070
Not only have fans eaten them up, but the
surprise nature of these releases has sparked

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:23.420
as much or more discussion than any expensive
marketing push could have; in addition, the

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.729
surprise drops have the added advantage of
being, you know, free.

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:32.830
Favreau, rightfully sensing that he had a
breakout character on his hands with "The

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:37.240
Child," decided to apply this strategy in
advance of The Mandalorian's release.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.590
It's safe to say that it worked; sure, Disney
could have easily included Baby Yoda in the

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.890
show's marketing, and the cute little bugger
may very well have taken the world by storm

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.660
in similar fashion if it had.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:53.810
But The Mandalorian, the first ever live-action
TV series set in the Star Wars universe, had

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:59.009
already built a strong buzz just for being
the first of its kind, and by virtue of being

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:03.700
the most high-profile original offering available
at the launch of Disney+.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:08.369
Favreau and the Mouse House basically gambled
that all eyes were going to be on the series

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:13.560
in any event, and that gamble paid off; little
Baby Yoda's reveal at the end of that first

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.670
episode melted hearts, sure, but it was also
a stunning surprise that we're pretty sure

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.650
no one saw coming.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.819
"This is what was causing all the fuss?"

00:02:24.819 --> 00:02:29.670
For one thing, it was only the second time
in Star Wars history that another member of

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.550
Yoda's mysterious species had been introduced.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.640
For another, it was an insane plot wrinkle,
instantly altering the trajectory of the titular

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.849
bounty hunter., fans were just blindsided
by all of that cuteness; if they had known

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:46.830
it was coming, it still would have been cool,
but the fact that it was a complete surprise

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.740
made it the kind of "holy crap" moment that
generates buzz on the level that no mere marketing

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:52.840
can accomplish.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:59.510
Look, $2.7 million is a lot of money by any
stretch, and the question has to be asked:

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:04.250
did Disney make the right decision, or should
the studio have cashed in using a more conventional

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.580
marketing campaign to introduce Baby Yoda?

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:11.269
Now that we've posed the query, let us answer
with a hearty laugh and the assertion that

00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:15.420
yes, the Mouse House absolutely made the right
choice.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.040
First of all, it stands to reason that including
Baby Yoda in the marketing push for The Mandalorian

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.370
may have set Disney back a comparable amount
of cash.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:27.420
The show's shooting schedule may have had
to be shuffled around to make sure that certain

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.319
shots would be available for marketing materials,
different one-sheets from the ones we got

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:36.010
would have to have been produced, and additional
funds would have to have been shelled out

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.300
to advertising types to develop a marketing
strategy for the little tyke, just off the

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.530
top of our heads.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:45.560
Second, the fact that toys weren't available
for the holiday season doesn't mean that those

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.260
who want them won't purchase them when they
are available.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:52.810
Heck, when Baby Yoda plushies showed up for
pre-order on Disney's online store, the allotted

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:56.680
number initially made available sold out in
a matter of hours.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:02.250
Disney was prepared for the character's popularity;
by the time Baby Yoda action figures and toys

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:07.360
are widely available between March and May
of 2020, everybody who wants one will be able

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.830
to get one, and that basically means literally
everybody.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:17.400
Finally: $2.7 million may be a lot of money,
but to Disney, it's freaking pocket change.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.870
This is the studio that released Avengers:
Endgame last spring, and that flick made $2.7

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:23.870
billion.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:29.139
The movie was one of six Mouse House releases
to make more than a billion bucks in 2019.

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:34.819
Its theme parks and merchandise generate billions
in revenue every year; Disney+ picked up 10

00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:37.909
million subscribers on its first day.

00:04:37.909 --> 00:04:39.599
Disney is doing just fine.

00:04:39.599 --> 00:04:44.479
No, we're thinking that the approach to Baby
Yoda's marketing was absolute genius, and

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:49.220
it's all down to a pleasant conversation that
Favreau and Glover had, discussing Beyoncé

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.220
on their coffee break.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:55.659
Now, if Queen Bey's next surprise video would
feature a dancing Baby Yoda, we'd really have

00:04:55.659 --> 00:04:56.659
something.

00:04:56.659 --> 00:04:59.860
We're pretty sure we're the first to have
that idea; we'll take a nice fruit basket

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.849
as a thank you or $2.7 million.

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:04.349
Whichever is easiest.

